{"key":"enterprise/T1546.012","id":"T1546.012","name":"Image File Execution Options Injection","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1546","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may establish persistence and/or elevate privileges by executing malicious content triggered by Image File Execution Options (IFEO) debuggers. IFEOs enable a developer to attach a debugger to an application. When a process is created, a debugger present in an application’s IFEO will be prepended to the application’s name, effectively launching the new process under the debugger (e.g., C:\\dbg\\ntsd.exe -g notepad.exe). IFEOs can be set…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/012","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--6d4a7fb3-5a24-42be-ae61-6728a2b581f6","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.640Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0056","name":"Windows Registry Key Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0056","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--7f70fae7-a68d-4730-a83a-f260b9606129","page":"telemetry/DC0056/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0422","name":"Detection Strategy for IFEO Injection on Windows","url":"https://attack.mitre.org